00:02:44.372 --> 00:02:45.582
Of the bubble economy at the end of the 1980s.

00:02:45.606 --> 00:02:47.884
Apparently, it suddenly collapsed last night.

00:02:47.908 --> 00:02:49.720
The incident is expected
to ignite further debate

00:02:49.744 --> 00:02:51.388
--Was that your mother on the phone?
--over what actions should be taken

00:02:51.412 --> 00:02:53.457
--Yeah. --What did she say?
--with regard to derelict buildings like this...

00:02:53.481 --> 00:02:57.294
--Oh, nothing. She feels she has to call me every now and then.
--Why did a derelict building suddenly collapse

00:02:57.318 --> 00:02:58.295
--Hmm...
--for no apparent reason?

00:02:58.319 --> 00:02:59.262
"On the brink of disaster! Building Collapses!” -——Hmm...
--for no apparent reason?

00:02:59.286 --> 00:03:01.732
"On the brink of disaster! Building Collapses!”
The second-story roof of a residence

00:03:01.756 --> 00:03:02.299
"On the brink of disaster! Building Collapses!”
located about 200 meters from the apartment building

00:03:02.323 --> 00:03:03.967
located about 200 meters
from the apartment building

00:03:03.991 --> 00:03:08.939
--also collapsed around the same time.
--What was that about last night?

00:03:08.963 --> 00:03:12.409
I thought we'd become at least a little closer...

00:03:12.433 --> 00:03:16.880
Oh, well, we did it to save Kato anyway...

00:03:16.904 --> 00:03:18.181
Dammit.

00:03:18.205 --> 00:03:20.884
We have been following the
story of two high school boys

00:03:20.908 --> 00:03:22.853
who went missing in the subway,

00:03:22.877 --> 00:03:24.788
leaving behind nothing but an adult magazine.

00:03:24.812 --> 00:03:28.291
--Man, they're still talking about that?
--Now, the latest news on that story...

00:03:28.315 --> 00:03:33.697
And now it's become the high school
students "with the adult magazine”!

00:03:33.721 --> 00:03:37.000
They're talking about you, right?

00:03:37.024 --> 00:03:38.468
I knew it...

00:03:38.492 --> 00:03:42.305
I didn't think Kato would
be reading those things...

00:03:42.329 --> 00:03:43.974
Oh, and how do you know?

00:03:43.998 --> 00:03:48.345
Because he's staying at a relative's
house with his little brother, right?

00:03:48.369 --> 00:03:50.580
I don't think he has stuff like that.

00:03:50.604 --> 00:03:52.683
What makes you so sure?

00:03:52.707 --> 00:03:56.286
Kato must have a lot of stuff to worry about.

00:03:56.310 --> 00:03:58.422
He has to take care of his brother,

00:03:58.446 --> 00:04:02.592
and then when we're all at that apartment,
he worries about us so much...

00:04:02.616 --> 00:04:06.163
I guess he's just a really caring guy.

00:04:06.187 --> 00:04:07.731
He just likes to buttin on
everyone's business, that's all.

00:04:07.755 --> 00:04:09.866
Don't you talk about him that way!

00:04:09.890 --> 00:04:11.401
If it weren't for him,

00:04:11.425 --> 00:04:13.603
where would we all be now, huh?

00:04:13.627 --> 00:04:16.473
Yeah, but I'm the one who
was able to pull the trigger...

00:04:16.497 --> 00:04:18.475
Yeah, that's true... But, still...

00:04:18.499 --> 00:04:22.646
Now that I've been there twice,
| understand something really well.

00:04:22.670 --> 00:04:26.283
Being caring isn't enough to survive there...

00:04:26.307 --> 00:04:28.919
Kato can talk all he wants about
all of us going back together,

00:04:28.943 --> 00:04:31.105
but it's not that easy.

00:04:40.821 --> 00:04:42.499
Yeah, I guess you're right...

00:04:42.523 --> 00:04:45.969
I think so, too.

00:04:45.993 --> 00:04:49.306
I really do agree with you.

00:04:49.330 --> 00:04:51.594
Well, that was good.

00:04:53.968 --> 00:04:55.800
What the heck's with her?

00:05:01.308 --> 00:05:01.518
"Fresh Mix Sandwich 170 yen Total
170 yen Paid 200 yen Change due 30 yen”

00:05:01.542 --> 00:05:03.620
"Fresh Mix Sandwich 170 yen Total 170 yen
Paid 200 yen Change due 30 yen” Thank you.

00:05:03.644 --> 00:05:04.270
"Fresh Mix Sandwich 170 yen Total
170 yen Paid 200 yen Change due 30 yen”

00:05:07.381 --> 00:05:09.543
Look what you've done!

00:05:13.020 --> 00:05:16.299
I won't let you get away with this!

00:05:16.323 --> 00:05:18.301
How dare you ask me for breakfast?!

00:05:18.325 --> 00:05:22.005
I know you came in the house yesterday
with your shoes all muddy again!

00:05:22.029 --> 00:05:24.541
The foyer is a mess!

00:05:24.565 --> 00:05:25.842
Ayumu!

00:05:25.866 --> 00:05:27.911
Did he do something?

00:05:27.935 --> 00:05:33.049
This good-for-nothing kid has the nerve
to ask me for breakfast after what he did!

00:05:33.073 --> 00:05:36.186
What do you think? Am I wrong here?

00:05:36.210 --> 00:05:38.770
If you think I'm wrong,
why don't you say something?!

00:05:40.114 --> 00:05:43.982
Well? Answer me!

00:05:47.721 --> 00:05:50.834
I have nothing to feed either of you!

00:05:50.858 --> 00:05:55.172
I just bought breakfast for Ayumu, so...

00:05:55.196 --> 00:05:57.494
Shut up!

00:06:00.334 --> 00:06:02.712
Please stop! That's enough...

00:06:02.736 --> 00:06:04.548
Huh? Did you just say something?

00:06:04.572 --> 00:06:07.317
Are you planning to give me lip?

00:06:07.341 --> 00:06:09.753
Please stop it.

00:06:09.777 --> 00:06:11.721
Are you defying me?

00:06:11.745 --> 00:06:14.858
Who the hell do you think you are? Eh?

00:06:14.882 --> 00:06:17.494
Stop it...

00:06:17.518 --> 00:06:19.296
What kind of look is that?

00:06:19.320 --> 00:06:21.364
Please stop it!

00:06:21.388 --> 00:06:26.019
If you hit him one more time... I'll...

00:06:31.398 --> 00:06:33.176
What are...?

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:35.245
If you keep it up...

00:06:35.269 --> 00:06:38.148
...I don't know what I might do!

00:06:38.172 --> 00:06:40.283
Stop it, big brother!

00:06:40.307 --> 00:06:44.888
That's enough! Please, just stop!

00:06:44.912 --> 00:06:47.157
Get... Get out!

00:06:47.181 --> 00:06:50.845
Both of you, get the hell
out of this house, now!

00:06:58.158 --> 00:07:00.718
We... We'll do that.

00:07:02.963 --> 00:07:05.809
When AC equals 1,

00:07:05.833 --> 00:07:09.913
--BC equals root 3...
--Kishimoto...

00:07:09.937 --> 00:07:14.284
He was trying his hardest,
not letting even one person die...

00:07:14.308 --> 00:07:18.321
Kato's the kind of guy who values the
lives of everyone around him equally.

00:07:18.345 --> 00:07:21.224
Crap... Here we go again.

00:07:21.248 --> 00:07:25.295
He's caring and strong... like no other...

00:07:25.319 --> 00:07:28.999
That's right... He's like no other.

00:07:29.023 --> 00:07:30.967
<i>What the hell is this?</i>

00:07:30.991 --> 00:07:34.004
What is she talking about looking like that?

00:07:34.028 --> 00:07:35.472
--180 degrees...
--Excuse me!

00:07:35.496 --> 00:07:38.625
--Yes?
--Kurono's got a hard-on again!

00:07:39.633 --> 00:07:42.534
Kurono... Again?

00:07:49.376 --> 00:07:51.755
Hoo, boy...

00:07:51.779 --> 00:07:55.292
--Excuse me.
--Oh, pardon me.

00:07:55.316 --> 00:07:58.995
That same guy stole our books again...

00:07:59.019 --> 00:08:03.286
Supposedly, he's been
selling the books he shoplifts.

00:08:05.359 --> 00:08:07.137
Well, now, how can I help you?

00:08:07.161 --> 00:08:10.140
Have you got the book I ordered the other day?

00:08:10.164 --> 00:08:12.633
Oh, let me check...

00:08:15.970 --> 00:08:17.247
What's your name, Ma'am?

00:08:17.271 --> 00:08:20.116
Sakuraoka. Sei Sakuraoka.

00:08:20.140 --> 00:08:23.887
Wow, what a pretty name...

00:08:23.911 --> 00:08:25.622
I wonder what kanji she uses to write it.

00:08:25.646 --> 00:08:28.792
Let me see... Oh, this one.

00:08:28.816 --> 00:08:31.728
Miranda Foster's Labyrinth, right?

00:08:31.752 --> 00:08:34.130
Ah, I'm sorry. Looks like it hasn't come in yet.

00:08:34.154 --> 00:08:38.101
It's kind of hard to get it in, since they never
did another printing after the first edition...

00:08:38.125 --> 00:08:39.669
Do you have any idea
when you'll be able to get it?

00:08:39.693 --> 00:08:44.841
Hmm... Hopefully by the end of next week.

00:08:44.865 --> 00:08:47.277
I'll call you when it comes in.

00:08:47.301 --> 00:08:49.702
That'd be great. Thanks.

00:08:55.476 --> 00:08:57.287
It's a frickin' toy!

00:08:57.311 --> 00:08:58.755
No, it's not.

00:08:58.779 --> 00:09:00.156
Where'd you get it?

00:09:00.180 --> 00:09:03.593
Well, it's kind of a long story...

00:09:03.617 --> 00:09:05.795
Long story?

00:09:05.819 --> 00:09:08.465
Hah! This piece of shit?

00:09:08.489 --> 00:09:12.035
Can I use it as the payment for this month?
You know, like instead of money?

00:09:12.059 --> 00:09:13.770
You shittin' me?

00:09:13.794 --> 00:09:16.906
Who the hell'd want this
piece of garbage, ya moron?!

00:09:16.930 --> 00:09:18.908
So, are you saying no?

00:09:18.932 --> 00:09:23.460
What, you ain't got the money?
Eh? C'mon, give it up!

00:09:24.705 --> 00:09:27.217
You planning on taking it to the grave?

00:09:27.241 --> 00:09:29.686
Huh? What did you just say?

00:09:29.710 --> 00:09:34.580
You don't need money.
Cuz'you'll be dead real soon.

00:09:55.135 --> 00:09:58.730
No one can fuck with me now!

00:10:03.510 --> 00:10:08.209
Hey, you'll fall if you keep running
around like that! Come on, be careful!

00:10:11.718 --> 00:10:13.982
Okay, time to go home!

00:10:22.262 --> 00:10:24.474
This is it.

00:10:24.498 --> 00:10:27.377
I saved up enough money
for it working part-time.

00:10:27.401 --> 00:10:30.371
This is our home from now on.

00:10:37.945 --> 00:10:40.812
Yay! We did it! We did it!

00:10:44.451 --> 00:10:46.463
<i>I'm sorry, Ayumu...</i>

00:10:46.487 --> 00:10:48.431
Huh? About what?

00:10:48.455 --> 00:10:51.167
If only I could've saved up sooner...

00:10:51.191 --> 00:10:53.203
Hey, it's alright!

00:10:53.227 --> 00:10:56.339
From today on, I don't need
to put up with her hitting me...

00:10:56.363 --> 00:10:58.092
That's all that matters.

00:10:59.466 --> 00:11:01.366
<i>I'm so...</i>

00:11:03.170 --> 00:11:04.981
Let's make it together, big bro!

00:11:05.005 --> 00:11:06.883
I'll get a job soon, too!

00:11:06.907 --> 00:11:10.420
Don't be silly! You have to go to school!

00:11:10.444 --> 00:11:13.256
Hey, how about our futons?

00:11:13.280 --> 00:11:15.758
My friend has a couple
of old futons he'll give us.

00:11:15.782 --> 00:11:17.360
I need to go get them now.

00:11:17.384 --> 00:11:18.995
I'm coming, too.

00:11:19.019 --> 00:11:20.897
<i>They're too heavy for you to
carry by yourself, aren't they?</i>

00:11:20.921 --> 00:11:22.398
I'll be fine.

00:11:22.422 --> 00:11:24.400
You stay home and watch TV.

00:11:24.424 --> 00:11:26.169
You've been wanting to
watch some anime, right?

00:11:26.193 --> 00:11:27.871
Can I really?!

00:11:27.895 --> 00:11:29.973
Yup. Now you can watch it
every day if you want to!

00:11:29.997 --> 00:11:31.556
Thanks!

00:11:33.600 --> 00:11:36.246
Here's the change.

00:11:36.270 --> 00:11:38.848
You know, I can cook as
long as it's nothing fancy.

00:11:38.872 --> 00:11:41.718
It's too expensive to keep buying
dinner at the convenience stores.

00:11:41.742 --> 00:11:44.020
Don't worry about it.

00:11:44.044 --> 00:11:46.890
It's not like we're living together or anything...

00:11:46.914 --> 00:11:48.658
Do you want me to start cooking tomorrow?

00:11:48.682 --> 00:11:50.560
I said it's okay!

00:11:50.584 --> 00:11:52.262
Why are you so mad?

00:11:52.286 --> 00:11:54.030
I'm not mad.

00:11:54.054 --> 00:11:56.065
Yes you are, Kurono.

00:11:56.089 --> 00:11:59.423
I bet you wouldn't be bugging
me like this if I were Kato!

00:12:03.931 --> 00:12:04.707
Great.

00:12:04.731 --> 00:12:05.074
"Oversized Trash" "Do
not leave trash” Great.

00:12:05.098 --> 00:12:06.809
"Oversized Trash" "Do not
leave trash” They're still here.

00:12:06.833 --> 00:12:07.197
"Oversized Trash"
"Do not leave trash”

00:12:18.278 --> 00:12:21.658
I'll be making a little more
money starting next month, so...

00:12:21.682 --> 00:12:22.792
Really?

00:12:22.816 --> 00:12:25.361
You wanna move? To a bigger place?

00:12:25.385 --> 00:12:27.697
We don't have that kind of money.

00:12:27.721 --> 00:12:29.866
We'll be fine.

00:12:29.890 --> 00:12:31.367
Right...

00:12:31.391 --> 00:12:32.702
Hey!

00:12:32.726 --> 00:12:35.438
--Cut the bullshit!
--What?

00:12:35.462 --> 00:12:38.474
What the hell are you doing?
You know you're not producing milk!

00:12:38.498 --> 00:12:40.510
What else am I gonna do?!

00:12:40.534 --> 00:12:43.046
You'll buy yourself cigarettes,
but never buy milk for the baby!

00:12:43.070 --> 00:12:44.847
It's all my stupid husband's fault!

00:12:44.871 --> 00:12:46.716
What did you just say?

00:12:46.740 --> 00:12:48.818
I got a call from the construction site.

00:12:48.842 --> 00:12:51.054
They said none of you showed up for work.

00:12:51.078 --> 00:12:53.856
They also said not to bother coming anymore.

00:12:53.880 --> 00:12:57.339
Pathetic... They fired all four of you!

00:13:06.860 --> 00:13:09.172
You got this umbrella from your friend, too?

00:13:09.196 --> 00:13:11.608
Uh, yeah...

00:13:11.632 --> 00:13:13.343
You've got nice friends.

00:13:13.367 --> 00:13:15.144
I guess so...

00:13:15.168 --> 00:13:17.637
Okay, it's all done! Look!

00:13:18.839 --> 00:13:21.184
Cool! A.K.!

00:13:21.208 --> 00:13:25.088
I spent almost all the money getting this place.

00:13:25.112 --> 00:13:27.240
But I'll start saving up again.

00:13:28.282 --> 00:13:30.627
I'm gonna sleep with this tonight.

00:13:30.651 --> 00:13:32.428
Then you'll dream about the rain.

00:13:32.452 --> 00:13:34.464
That's okay.

00:13:34.488 --> 00:13:36.957
Now I can't wait for it to rain!

00:13:40.594 --> 00:13:44.574
Okay, I'm going to sleep.

00:13:44.598 --> 00:13:45.875
Ayumu.

00:13:45.899 --> 00:13:47.310
What?

00:13:47.334 --> 00:13:50.235
Uh... Never mind.

00:13:53.073 --> 00:13:58.121
I saw this beautiful girl when I was killing
time at the bookstore this afternoon.

00:13:58.145 --> 00:14:00.890
Huh? What the heck do I care?

00:14:00.914 --> 00:14:04.227
Her name was Sei Sakuraoka.

00:14:04.251 --> 00:14:07.597
It looked like she had ordered
some book called Labyrinth.

00:14:07.621 --> 00:14:09.799
How about that...

00:14:09.823 --> 00:14:15.338
All I've been reading are study guides
and story collections of masterworks.

00:14:15.362 --> 00:14:18.474
So it made me wonder what
kind of book this Labyrinth is...

00:14:18.498 --> 00:14:21.544
Hey, Kurono, do you read books like that?

00:14:21.568 --> 00:14:24.833
Not really. I'm not really into that stuff.

00:14:27.574 --> 00:14:30.441
I wonder how Kato's doing...

00:14:35.782 --> 00:14:38.127
What are you talking about?

00:14:38.151 --> 00:14:40.630
I'm not saying I want you to give up your bike.

00:14:40.654 --> 00:14:43.232
And even if I did,
you'd never listen to me anyway.

00:14:43.256 --> 00:14:45.501
Where were you last night?
What were you doing?

00:14:45.525 --> 00:14:47.270
What do you mean?

00:14:47.294 --> 00:14:49.339
You never came back
after you went to get milk!

00:14:49.363 --> 00:14:51.774
I don't know how many times
I tried calling you on your cell!

00:14:51.798 --> 00:14:53.609
Why did you turn off your phone?

00:14:53.633 --> 00:14:56.879
| was out-of-area!

00:14:56.903 --> 00:14:58.381
Yeah, right!

00:14:58.405 --> 00:15:02.118
| bet you were out fucking around
with your boy Haruya again.

00:15:02.142 --> 00:15:05.221
All your buddies' cell phones
were off last night, too!

00:15:05.245 --> 00:15:07.690
That's not what I was doing!

00:15:07.714 --> 00:15:09.926
Then why did you turn off your phone?

00:15:09.950 --> 00:15:12.829
Even if I explained it to you,
you wouldn't understand!

00:15:12.853 --> 00:15:14.297
Don't give me that bullshit!

00:15:14.321 --> 00:15:16.199
No! Don't you give me your bullshit!

00:15:16.223 --> 00:15:19.635
I... I spent the whole damn night...

00:15:19.659 --> 00:15:23.391
So there were that many good-looking
girls out there, huh?! Is that it?

00:15:27.434 --> 00:15:30.780
I bet Kato has a lot to worry about.

00:15:30.804 --> 00:15:32.148
Give me a break!

00:15:32.172 --> 00:15:36.386
You were acting like you agreed
with me a little this morning!

00:15:36.410 --> 00:15:40.456
He was trying really hard
so all of us could survive...

00:15:40.480 --> 00:15:46.229
But if you think about it, he didn't
end up being all that helpful...

00:15:46.253 --> 00:15:48.531
What? Why do you say stuff like that?

00:15:48.555 --> 00:15:49.966
It's not true!

00:15:49.990 --> 00:15:51.467
Oh, yeah?

00:15:51.491 --> 00:15:54.504
There's one for every person in this world...

00:15:54.528 --> 00:15:55.638
One what?

00:15:55.662 --> 00:15:57.907
I'm saying everyone has some role to play.

00:15:57.931 --> 00:15:59.475
What?

00:15:59.499 --> 00:16:02.011
Like how you beat the aliens

00:16:02.035 --> 00:16:04.547
while Kato concentrated
on protecting everyone.

00:16:04.571 --> 00:16:06.616
I mean things like that.

00:16:06.640 --> 00:16:08.184
Whatever...

00:16:08.208 --> 00:16:13.044
I think that... both of you are great.

00:16:14.815 --> 00:16:20.845
Kato's the kind of guy who values the
lives of everyone around him equally.

00:16:21.988 --> 00:16:26.736
He's caring and strong... like no other.

00:16:26.760 --> 00:16:29.472
Yeah, he's different from everyone else.

00:16:29.496 --> 00:16:31.307
What the hell are you trying to say?!

00:16:31.331 --> 00:16:33.876
--What?
--What the hell are you trying to say?!

00:16:33.900 --> 00:16:35.545
What the hell is your problem?

00:16:35.569 --> 00:16:42.151
You say all that just because you
couldn't reach me for one frickin' night?

00:16:42.175 --> 00:16:44.821
Fine! Prove you weren't out
doing anything like that last night!

00:16:44.845 --> 00:16:46.823
Well? Can you?

00:16:46.847 --> 00:16:48.024
I was...

00:16:48.048 --> 00:16:50.359
I was... just...

00:16:50.383 --> 00:16:51.627
What the heck is that?

00:16:51.651 --> 00:16:53.963
Trying to intimidate me with a toy gun?

00:16:53.987 --> 00:16:55.231
You're so stupid!

00:16:55.255 --> 00:16:57.600
Bitch! I'll fuckin' kill you!

00:16:57.624 --> 00:17:01.185
Okay, go ahead! Shoot me! C'mon!

00:17:02.696 --> 00:17:04.207
This is bullshit!

00:17:04.231 --> 00:17:06.909
How are we supposed to live with no money?

00:17:06.933 --> 00:17:11.481
Who's going to give a lowlife biker
like you a job in this economy?

00:17:11.505 --> 00:17:14.851
C'mon, answer me! C'mon!

00:17:14.875 --> 00:17:16.552
Make up your mind, will you?

00:17:16.576 --> 00:17:18.888
You're so indecisive, you know that?

00:17:18.912 --> 00:17:23.726
I didn't mean to sound that way...

00:17:23.750 --> 00:17:27.497
You move into my place right out of the blue,
but you don't even let me touch you!

00:17:27.521 --> 00:17:30.233
It's always "Kato, Kato, Kato"!

00:17:30.257 --> 00:17:32.735
Wait a minute...

00:17:32.759 --> 00:17:35.471
"Kato, Kato"!

00:17:35.495 --> 00:17:39.308
I knew what you were thinking last night
when you asked Kato if he lives by himself.

00:17:39.332 --> 00:17:41.244
Okay... And so what?

00:17:41.268 --> 00:17:45.214
You were asking because you
wanted to live with him, not me, right?

00:17:45.238 --> 00:17:48.317
I didn't say that.

00:17:48.341 --> 00:17:50.319
You might as well have!

00:17:50.343 --> 00:17:52.588
You're just using me!

00:17:52.612 --> 00:17:54.423
Give me a break!

00:17:54.447 --> 00:17:55.658
What the hell am I doing with you, anyway?

00:17:55.682 --> 00:17:59.084
Get out! Just get out now!

00:18:06.326 --> 00:18:09.171
What the hell am I doing?

00:18:09.195 --> 00:18:12.241
I'm letting you stay here
and eat my food for free!

00:18:12.265 --> 00:18:15.211
I'm a complete fool!

00:18:15.235 --> 00:18:17.246
You're right...

00:18:17.270 --> 00:18:21.229
Keeping up my scores at school
doesn't mean anything, I guess...

00:18:22.709 --> 00:18:26.789
I don't understand how the world works at all...

00:18:26.813 --> 00:18:30.226
I guess it's not like cooking for you
will make it all better. Will it?

00:18:30.250 --> 00:18:33.162
Shit, I crossed the line... What should I do now?

00:18:33.186 --> 00:18:35.298
You're right, Kurono.

00:18:35.322 --> 00:18:38.334
I know things can't be that convenient.

00:18:38.358 --> 00:18:40.336
Whoa, hold on!

00:18:40.360 --> 00:18:44.006
But there's one thing I want you to understand.

00:18:44.030 --> 00:18:49.211
I... I really do think you're great.

00:18:49.235 --> 00:18:51.247
What?

00:18:51.271 --> 00:18:52.815
I'm serious.

00:18:52.839 --> 00:18:58.220
You're a lot different from Kato, but... well...

00:18:58.244 --> 00:19:01.475
Shit... What do I do now?

00:19:04.718 --> 00:19:07.496
Hey, it's that same dude from the other day...

00:19:07.520 --> 00:19:10.800
Oh, yeah! The milk guy, right?

00:19:10.824 --> 00:19:12.952
Is he a ghost or something?

00:19:14.327 --> 00:19:17.820
What am I doing this for?

00:19:22.035 --> 00:19:25.005
That's one dumb daddy, huh?

00:19:31.845 --> 00:19:35.124
Look at this dumb-ass! That's a toy!

00:19:35.148 --> 00:19:37.326
Moron!

00:19:37.350 --> 00:19:40.429
Hey, let's kill him one more time!

00:19:40.453 --> 00:19:44.967
Why? What the hell am I doing?

00:19:44.991 --> 00:19:48.237
Tell me why, Gantz!

00:19:48.261 --> 00:19:54.710
Do you think there's like a bomb or
something planted in each of our heads?

00:19:54.734 --> 00:19:57.829
Gantz? What the hell is that?

00:20:06.513 --> 00:20:10.279
Huh? What the hell's with him?

00:20:13.953 --> 00:20:17.333
Hey! I'm lactating! I can breastfeed now!

00:20:17.357 --> 00:20:20.703
Come home right now! I can feed our baby!

00:20:20.727 --> 00:20:26.257
No need for me anymore, then...

00:20:33.006 --> 00:20:35.818
I'msorry... I'm sorry...

00:20:35.842 --> 00:20:39.622
I'il... I'lmove out.

00:20:39.646 --> 00:20:43.708
Thank you for everything. Goodbye.

00:20:46.753 --> 00:20:50.519
But there's one thing I want you to understand.

00:20:54.027 --> 00:20:58.841
I... I really do think you're great.

00:20:58.865 --> 00:21:00.142
I'm serious.

00:21:00.166 --> 00:21:04.797
You're a lot different from Kato, but... well...

00:21:06.806 --> 00:21:13.940
Hajimari wa dare demo junshin muku na baby

00:21:18.418 --> 00:21:25.449
Nigai mi kajitte mo
kujikecha dame yo walk straight

00:21:29.996 --> 00:21:37.996
Satta koto da kedo
ame no naka zukizuki itamu yo

00:21:44.110 --> 00:21:46.355
I'm lonely as floating ice

00:21:46.379 --> 00:21:51.193
Yaseta yubi ni kiss o shite

00:21:51.217 --> 00:21:57.900
Naita anata o omoidasu yo

00:21:57.924 --> 00:22:02.772
Kore de owari da to shite mo

00:22:02.796 --> 00:22:07.676
Saigo no kiss wa wasurenai yo

00:22:07.700 --> 00:22:15.700
Wasurenai yo... Wasurenai yo...

00:22:19.612 --> 00:22:27.612
Kare no kiss o wasurenai yo

00:22:37.096 --> 00:22:40.342
Gantz, locked windows, locked doors,

00:22:40.366 --> 00:22:42.745
Tokyo Tower, strange people, an annoying song,

00:22:42.769 --> 00:22:43.712
"Your lives are now ovol, you bastards. What you do with vyour new lives iz for me
to decide. So there you have it."” Tokyo Tower, strange peoplfe, an annoying song,

